# .githooks/leak-patterns -- canonical regex list for the leak-scan trio
#
# Consumed by:
#   - .githooks/pre-commit         (staged-diff scan, local)
#   - .githooks/pre-push           (pushed-range scan, local)
#   - .github/workflows/leak-check.yml (tracked-tree scan, CI)
#
# One extended-regex token per line. `#` comments and blank lines are ignored
# by the readers (`grep -v '^\s*\(#\|$\)'`). The tokens are OR-joined into a
# single alternation before being handed to `grep -E`.
#
# Editing this file changes ALL THREE scanners at once -- that is the whole
# point (drift between them was Issue #12). Keep tokens strict enough not to
# false-positive on legitimate prefix-validation code (`tok.startswith("ghp_")`
# etc.), which is why token bodies require >=20 chars.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GitHub tokens (personal, OAuth, server, user, fine-grained)
ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
gho_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
ghs_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
ghu_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{40,}

# Third-party API tokens
hf_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}

# Structured secrets
-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----
eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}

# Hardcoded-credential idiom (password = "literal", etc.).
# NOTE: no `(?i)` inline flag -- git grep -E is POSIX ERE and rejects it.
# All three scanners run this list with `-i` (case-insensitive) at the call
# site, so alphabetic tokens here should be written lower-case.
(password|passwd|secret|api_key|apikey|token)[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*["'][^"'{$<]{8,}["']

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PII
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

leguillaume
lmlgg
@gmail\.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# internal identifiers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

MASTER_PLAN
192\.168\.86\.(31|23|77|219)
192\.168\.0\.100
